course: dictionary
lesson: 8116
title: One word, more than one job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a doing word or a naming word. Repair is one of them. To repair something means to fix it when it is broken or damaged. «Muscles repair the tiny strains of the day» tells you that the body mends small damage while you sleep.
explain: A repair can also be a naming word, meaning the work of fixing, or the place where the fixing was done. «Dad paid for the repair» is about the job, not the action. Read the words around it to see which job the word is doing.
explain: Some phrases have their own meanings. «Beyond repair» means too badly damaged to be fixed, as in «smashed beyond repair». «In good repair» means in good condition, so the thing works well. Do not try to work these out word by word.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word. In «repairing cushions», try fix: fixing cushions makes sense, so repairing means mending. This is the same check you used for other hard words.
fact: Repair as a doing word means to fix something that is broken or damaged.
fact: Repair as a naming word means the work of fixing, or the place that was fixed.
fact: «In good repair» means in good condition.
fact: «Beyond repair» means too damaged to be fixed.
fact: Mending things instead of throwing them away helps the planet.
exercise: «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, smashed beyond repair.» What does beyond repair mean? | Sitting in a shop window | *Too damaged to be fixed | Full of sardine tins | Painted again with a brush
exercise: «Rat and Mole were repairing cushions» before the boating season. What does repairing mean here? | Buying new cushions for the boat | Throwing them away | *Fixing them so they can be used again | Painting them bright red
exercise: In «Dad paid for the repair», what does repair mean? | A kind of holiday | *The work of fixing something | To paint something bright | To break something on purpose
test: Find and copy the word that means fix in: «Muscles repair the tiny strains of the day.» | *repair | muscles | strains | day
test: «The bike was in good repair after the mechanic finished.» What does in good repair mean? | Very quiet | Being sold cheaply | Wrapped up in paper | *In good condition
exam: During sleep, «the body repairs used muscles», so what does repairs mean in this sentence? | Throws them away | Stretches them for a long time | Makes them smaller | *Mends them after they have been used
